From: hzyitc <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Mar 2026 15:44:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: use request_firmware_direct() to avoid
 userspace helper timeout

The NPU driver loads before rootfs (squashfs) is mounted. When
CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER=y (pulled in by kmod-leds-lp5523 via
CONFIG_ALL_KMODS=y), request_firmware() sends a uevent and waits 60s
for a userspace helper that doesn't exist yet, then times out with
-ETIMEDOUT causing the probe to fail.

Use request_firmware_direct() which skips the userspace fallback path.
The firmware will still be found via the kernel's built-in firmware
search paths once rootfs is available (via deferred probe).

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/22697
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/22709
Signed-off-by: hzyitc <hzyitc@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@ static int airoha_npu_run_firmware(struc
 	if (fw_name)
 		name = fw_name;
 
-	ret = request_firmware(&fw, name, dev);
+	ret = request_firmware_direct(&fw, name, dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
